103:## Require a pull request before merging
131:{% ifversion repo-rules-merge-type %}
132:Optionally, you can require a merge type of merge, squash, or rebase. This means the targeted branches may only be merged based on the allowed type. Additionally if the repository has disabled a merge method and the ruleset required a different method, the merge will be blocked. See [AUTOTITLE](/repositories/configuring-branches-and-merges-in-your-repository/configuring-pull-request-merges/about-merge-methods-on-github).

